            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, both [scroll and resize animations are done with side effects](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c87d3b73d763d4222cdef19323e6a2c4bee33013/doc/mini-animate.txt#L38-L43). And yes, scroll animation actually moves cursor to show smoother cursor transition. Plus sometimes it is necessary to move cursor to show intermediate window view, as only view which contains cursor can be set.\r\n\r\nThe solution of this issue can be something along the line of [this suggestion](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c87d3b73d763d4222cdef19323e6a2c4bee33013/doc/mini-animate.txt#L277-L292) for `n` keymap which centers current line and opens folds.\r\n\r\nClosing as scroll and resize animation indeed need extra work to play nicely with other plugins/functionality (if at all possible).",
